A TCG op that tells whether every byte of a vector has its top bit set,
so patch 11's lane check branches on a register instead of a round trip
through env.

Every inlined SSE instruction (sse-fast.c.inc, sses_vec_insn) computes
its result in all lanes, checks them, and only then stores: the check
builds a vector `ok` whose lanes are all ones (acceptable) or all zeros
(the slow block must run). TCG had no way to test a vector from a
branch, so the mask went to env->sses_scratch with one 16-byte store,
came back as two 8-byte loads, was and'ed and compared with -1 -- six
instructions and a store-to-load dependency in front of every SSE op's
branch, on every guest that does SSE arithmetic.

vec_allsign_i32 (i32 out, one vector in, like patch 06's scalar cvt ops
take a vector-register operand) is 0 iff every byte of its operand has
its top bit set, nonzero otherwise; for a mask of all-ones / all-zero
lanes that is exactly "every lane passed":

  x86-64   vpmovmskb r32, xmm ; xor $0xffff          (TCG_TARGET_HAS: AVX1)
  aarch64  cmlt v31.16b, #0 ; uminv b31, v31.16b ;
           umov w, v31.b[0] ; eor #0xff               (V31: TCG_VEC_TMP0)

The check is then the op and a brcondi. Where the backend has no such op
the round trip stays as it was. tcg/optimize.c needs no case: like the
cvt ops it is an ordinary op with no folding.

The aarch64 half was not compiled on the host this patch was written on
(an x86-64 box): the Mac's build is its first, and the SSE battery there
is its test.

Measured on 3DMark 99 Max, claude98, 800x600x16, after patch 38: CPU
3DMarks 15389 -> 15940 (+4 %), the first-person test 17.1 -> 17.5 fps,
3DMarks 5932 -> 5950. SSE battery 546,425 lines identical on/off (the op
exercised on every packed check), x87, SMC and rep unchanged,
scripts/test.sh all 57/57.

Behind sse-fast, like the check it serves.

Test: tools/sse-guest-test.py (every packed op, its check and its slow
block, sse-fast on/off identical), the x87, SMC and rep batteries, and
3DMark 99 on claude98.

